            <ArticleTitle>Mastalgia: evaluation and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>213-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mastalgia, defined as breast pain, is a common, often distressing complaint among women. It is the most common breast-related complaint in primary care clinics, with a prevalence in working women of approximately 66%. An underlying fear of breast cancer is what prompts these patients to seek health care. A comprehensive history and thorough clinical breast exam is essential to evaluation. Once significant breast disease is ruled out, the majority of these patients respond to simple reassurance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
